Stakeholders’ relationship committee
The Stakeholders’ Relationship Committee of the Company is governed by the terms of reference adopted by the Board which are in line with the regulatory requirements mandated by the Act and the Listing Regulations.
The terms of reference of the Stakeholders’ Relationship Committee include:
a) Considering and resolving grievances of the security holders including complaints related to transfer / transmission of shares, non-receipt of annual report, non-receipt of declared dividends, general meetings, etc.;
b) Reviewing measures taken for effective exercise of voting rights by the shareholders;
c) Reviewing adherence to the service standards adopted in respect of various services rendered by the Company’s Registrar and Share Transfer Agents;
d) Reviewing various measures and initiatives taken for reducing the quantum of unclaimed dividends and ensuring timely receipt of dividend warrants / annual reports / statutory notices by the shareholders.
